From c4d9eb34cbb7f608a9eff7a1b5c4777f369cfac2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reilly Brogan <reilly@reillybrogan.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:55:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] visa: Fix link against flex 2.7

flex 2.7.8 gives the buffer struct of a C scanner that is compiled as C++
its own tag, yy_c_buffer_state, so that it no longer clashes with the struct
of a scanner generated with %option c++ (#831). The rename changes the
mangled name of the prefixed yy_delete_buffer(), and this file declares that
function itself, against its own YY_BUFFER_STATE typedef, so the declaration
stopped matching the definition and GenX_IR failed to link:

    ld.lld: error: undefined symbol: CISA_delete_buffer(yy_buffer_state*)

Name the struct tag flex uses for a C scanner compiled as C++.

Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-27
---
 visa/BuildCISAIRImpl.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/visa/BuildCISAIRImpl.cpp b/visa/BuildCISAIRImpl.cpp
index 56cfe12..20be95e 100644
--- a/visa/BuildCISAIRImpl.cpp
+++ b/visa/BuildCISAIRImpl.cpp
@@ -1550,7 +1550,7 @@ static void Stitch_Compiled_Units(G4_Kernel *mainFunc,
 }
 
 
-typedef struct yy_buffer_state *YY_BUFFER_STATE;
+typedef struct yy_c_buffer_state *YY_BUFFER_STATE;
 extern int CISAparse(CISA_IR_Builder *builder);
 extern YY_BUFFER_STATE CISA_scan_string(const char *yy_str);
 extern void CISA_delete_buffer(YY_BUFFER_STATE buf);
